# Soldering at the bench (decisions C17, C18, C22): the DIP into the vise
# on the turntable, legs up; the bending rig bends the resistor's lead
# 90 degrees and shears it to a 4 mm end, and arm A lays that end
# alongside pin 3's leg (a lap joint); pincer P1 comes in from the
# turntable's side and grips the lead -- the turntable now holds the
# resistor, and A lets go and goes; the turntable turns and rises to
# present the joint to station S1, whose iron touches it and whose own
# feeder feeds the solder; the iron backs away, the joint freezes; P1
# lets go and the resistor stays, soldered on.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.1 at=12
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.1 at=17.2
lift A mm=60
bring A R1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=-0.934,0.356,0 lap=3.2
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=3
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P1
